<!-- =====================================================================
     PAGE 3: OUR PHILOSOPHY
     ====================================================================== -->
<div class="page page-break">
    <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 01</div>
        <h2>Our Philosophy</h2>
        <p>Before telling you what we do, it's important to understand what drives us.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="section-intro" style="font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.9; color: var(--text-light);">
        This document will feel different from most you've seen.
    </p>

    <p>You're probably used to companies that hide prices behind contact forms, catalogues that say everything and nothing at the same time, and a sales process where you're treated like royalty&hellip; right until you sign &mdash; and then forgotten.</p>

    <p>If you're comfortable with that, this might not be for you.</p>

    <p>But if you've ever felt that something about it isn't quite right &mdash; that it's unnecessarily complicated, opaque, or simply unfair &mdash; then take a few minutes.</p>

    <p><strong>Because you're not wrong. And yes, there is another way.</strong></p>

    <div style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin: 25px 0 20px 0;"></div>

    <p>We're not here to build just another system. We're here to rethink how these systems should work.</p>

    <p>Everything we design starts from the same idea: make it simpler, make it clearer, and make it capable of more than what's expected today.</p>

    <p>Because good technology doesn't just solve problems &mdash; it opens possibilities.</p>

    <p>And if that's true, then those possibilities shouldn't be locked behind plans, upgrades, or hidden conditions.</p>

    <div class="callout" style="border-left-color: var(--primary); background: #f0f1fa;">
        <strong>We don't believe in "premium features"</strong> that suddenly appear only when you pay more.<br>
        We don't believe in systems that promise everything, but include almost nothing.<br><br>
        <strong>We believe that once you're in, you should have the full picture.</strong>
    </div>

    <p>That doesn't mean you have to use everything. It means everything is there &mdash; available, transparent, and ready when you need it.</p>

    <p>There are no hidden tiers, no artificial feature restrictions, and no "unlock this to access that" logic.</p>

    <p><strong>Just one system, designed to be fully accessible from day one.</strong></p>

    <p style="margin-top: 25px; font-style: italic; color: var(--text-light); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 20px;">
        Most systems are built around what they allow.<br>
        Sapiens is built around what you want to achieve.
    </p>

    <!-- Easter egg for the curious ones -->
    <p style="margin-top: 30px; font-size: 8pt; color: #ddd; text-align: right;" title="You found it. Yes, we named it after Homo sapiens. Because tools should make us smarter, not the other way around.">*</p>

    <div class="page-footer">
        <span class="confidential">SapiensCore &bull; Confidential</span>
        <span>Page 3</span>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- =====================================================================
     PAGE 4: WHAT SAPIENS ACTUALLY IS
     ====================================================================== -->
<div class="page page-break">
    <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 02</div>
        <h2>What Sapiens Actually Is</h2>
        <p>One system. Everything connected. Nothing left behind.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="section-intro" style="font-size: 11.5pt; line-height: 1.9;">
        Sapiens is the system that connects and controls your entire operation.
    </p>

    <p>It brings together everything that usually lives in separate tools &mdash; games, payments, loyalty, and daily operations &mdash; into one platform that works in real time.</p>

    <p>For some, that means replacing everything with a single, unified solution.<br>
    For others, it means connecting what they already have and making it finally work together.</p>

    <p><strong>Sapiens is designed for both.</strong></p>

    <div style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin: 25px 0;"></div>

    <h3>Start from scratch, or integrate step by step</h3>

    <p>You can build your operation on top of Sapiens from day one.<br>
    Or you can integrate it into your existing setup and evolve at your own pace.</p>

    <p>There's no need to rebuild everything overnight.<br>
    There's no need to force a migration that doesn't make sense.</p>

    <p>You decide how far you want to go.</p>

    <p>What matters is that, behind the scenes, <strong>everything becomes connected.</strong></p>

    <p>So when a customer plays, the system knows.<br>
    When a payment happens, it's reflected instantly.<br>
    When you make a change, it applies everywhere.</p>

    <p>You're no longer managing disconnected pieces. You're managing one system.</p>

    <!-- Easter egg #2 -->
    <p style="font-size: 7pt; color: #e8e8e8; margin-top: 20px;" title="42. The answer is always 42.">// TODO: take over the world (right after lunch)</p>

    <div class="page-footer">
        <span class="confidential">SapiensCore &bull; Confidential</span>
