<!-- =====================================================================
     PAGE 7: BUILT FOR THE REAL WORLD
     ====================================================================== -->
<div class="page page-break">

    <h3>Built for the real world</h3>

    <p class="section-intro" style="font-size: 11pt;">
        Sapiens works both online and offline, at the same time.
    </p>

    <p>Let's be honest about the two easy paths &mdash; and why we didn't take either.</p>

    <p><strong>A 100% cloud solution</strong> would be so much easier for us to develop. Everything centralized, one deployment, no local infrastructure. It sounds modern and clean. Until the day the internet goes down &mdash; and your entire venue stops. Games don't start. Payments fail. Cards don't work. Your customers are standing there, and you're calling your ISP.</p>

    <p><strong>A mostly offline system with some online features</strong> would also be simpler. Everything runs locally, no dependency on connectivity. But you lose real-time visibility, remote monitoring, instant sync across locations, live analytics. You're running blind between manual syncs.</p>

    <p>Both approaches have critical weaknesses. Both are compromises that sacrifice something essential to make development easier.</p>

    <div class="callout" style="border-left-color: var(--primary); background: #f0f1fa;">
        <strong>We went with what we believe is the right way &mdash; which is, as usual, the hard one.</strong><br><br>
        A system that works both offline and online. Continuous real-time sync when connected. Full local operation when not. Automatic restoration when connectivity returns. Real-time alerts when something goes wrong.<br><br>
        Every location runs a local NUC server with full operational capability. Games, payments, loyalty cards &mdash; everything keeps working regardless of internet status. When connectivity is restored, data syncs automatically. No manual intervention. No lost transactions. No gap in your data.
    </div>

    <p><strong>Because real businesses don't stop when the internet does.</strong></p>

    <p>And that's the difference. Other systems choose the easy path and ask you to live with the trade-offs. We chose the hard path so you don't have to make that choice at all.</p>

    <div class="page-footer">
        <span class="confidential">SapiensCore &bull; Confidential</span>
        <span>Page 7</span>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- =====================================================================
     PAGE 5-6: LOYALTY CARD SYSTEM — BALANCE TYPES & TIERS
     ====================================================================== -->
<div class="page page-break">
    <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 03</div>
        <h2>Loyalty Card System</h2>
        <p>Balance types, tier engine, and intelligent credit management.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="section-intro">
        The loyalty card system is the financial backbone of SapiensCore. Every play session, every purchase, and every reward flows through the card system. Unlike simple stored-value cards, SapiensCore manages six distinct balance types simultaneously, each with its own business rules, consumption priority, and accounting treatment.
    </p>

    <div class="callout" style="border-left-color: var(--success); background: #f0faf0;">
        <strong>Your cards, your rules, zero lock-in.</strong> SapiensCore does not lock you into a proprietary card ecosystem. You can use <strong>whatever cards you want</strong>:

        <ul class="clean" style="margin-top: 8px; margin-bottom: 8px;">
            <li><strong>Bring your existing cards:</strong> If you already have NFC or RFID cards from another system, we can integrate them. Provide us with a few samples and we'll configure compatibility.</li>
            <li><strong>Buy from any provider you trust:</strong> If you have a card supplier you already work with &mdash; honestly, that's even better for us. It means you are fully independent. No dependency on SapiensCore for physical cards.</li>
            <li><strong>Buy from us at cost:</strong> If you prefer, we supply NFC/RFID cards at <strong>0.10 EUR per card</strong>. No markup, no hidden fees.</li>
            <li><strong>Free card testing tool:</strong> We provide a testing tool to validate cards from any provider &mdash; ensuring they work correctly with the system before you order in bulk. This service has no fee.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <h3>Six Balance Types</h3>
    <table class="data-table">
        <tr>
            <th>Balance</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Credit</strong></td>
            <td>Primary monetary balance loaded via cash or card payment. Subject to expiration policies if you wish to do so.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Credit-VAT</strong></td>
            <td>Credit where VAT is postponed until the moment of use. Tracked separately for tax compliance. See the dedicated Credit-VAT chapter &mdash; this is one of Sapiens' most important capabilities and that probably no one has ever told you.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Bonus</strong></td>
            <td>Promotional balance awarded as part of package deals. Free credit given to the customer &mdash; not purchased.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Courtesy</strong></td>
            <td>Complimentary balance for service recovery, VIP treatment, or staff use.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Time</strong></td>
            <td>Duration-based credit measured in seconds. Enables "unlimited play" (can still be limited for fair use and by game/game type) packages with configurable activation.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Tickets</strong></td>
            <td>Game-won tickets redeemable for prizes. Separate from monetary balances. Tracked per card with full audit trail.</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Intelligent Consumption Priority</h3>
    <p>When a customer plays a game, Sapiens automatically decides the order in which balances are consumed. The logic is designed to <strong>maximize your business</strong>:</p>

    <ul class="clean">
        <li><strong>Gifts first.</strong> Balances that were given for free are consumed before anything the customer paid for. This protects the customer's purchased credit and ensures your promotional spend is used before real revenue is touched.</li>
        <li><strong>Regular credit next.</strong> The money the customer actually paid &mdash; where VAT was already charged at the moment of top-up. Think of all pre-sapiens era.</li>
        <li><strong>Credit-VAT as last resort.</strong> Because the moment Credit-VAT is consumed, you become VAT-liable for that exact amount. So the system uses it only when there is no other alternative. This minimizes your tax obligations to the absolute legal minimum.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Sapiens manages all six balance types <strong>simultaneously on every card</strong>. A single transaction can consume multiple balance types at once &mdash; for example, 0.20 from bonus + 1.60 from credit in one play. All partial movements are calculated and applied automatically. Staff never make this decision. The system does.</p>

    <div class="highlight-box">
        <p><strong>Why this matters:</strong> This isn't just an accounting optimization &mdash; it's a business strategy. Customers see their purchased credit lasting longer because free balances are used first. Credit-VAT is protected until absolutely necessary, keeping your tax obligations correct and minimized. And because partial consumption across multiple balance types is automatic, there's no rounding, no approximation, no manual intervention &mdash; every cent is tracked to the correct balance, on every single transaction.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-footer">
        <span class="confidential">SapiensCore &bull; Confidential</span>
