</div>

<!-- =====================================================================
     VAT-POSTPONED CREDIT: THE FEATURE NO ONE ELSE OFFERS
     ====================================================================== -->
<div class="page page-break">
    <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 04</div>
        <h2>Credit-VAT: The Money You're Losing Without Knowing It</h2>
        <p>This might be the most important page in this document.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>The problem</h3>

    <p>When a customer tops up their loyalty card with 10 EUR, most systems charge VAT immediately &mdash; on the full amount, at the point of sale.</p>

    <p><strong>That is wrong.</strong></p>

    <p>A top-up is not a sale. It's credit. The customer is prepaying for future use. VAT should only be calculated &mdash; and declared to tax authorities &mdash; when that credit is actually <em>spent</em>. Not when it's loaded.</p>

    <p>This distinction sounds academic. It's not. It's money.</p>

    <div class="callout" style="border-left-color: var(--danger); background: #fdf2f2;">
        <strong>Here's a simple test you can do right now.</strong><br><br>
        Open the software you're currently using. Ask: how much credit is sitting on customer cards, unused?<br><br>
        Take that number. Calculate the VAT on it.<br><br>
        <strong>That's what you've already paid to the tax authorities &mdash; and you shouldn't have.</strong><br><br>
        That money is gone. It was declared as revenue, taxed, and paid. But the customer never used it. They might never use it. And you can't get it back.
    </div>

    <h3>Why no one else does this</h3>

    <p>Three reasons.</p>

    <p><strong>First, you need to deeply understand how these businesses actually operate.</strong> Not from a marketing slide &mdash; from the inside. How credit flows, how bonus is given, how partial plays work, how a customer can use credit for games today and food tomorrow. Most software companies have never worked at this level.</p>

    <p><strong>Second, it's genuinely hard to implement.</strong> Consider what actually happens:</p>

    <ul class="clean">
        <li>A customer tops up 10 EUR. They receive 10 EUR credit + 2 EUR free bonus.</li>
        <li>They play a game that costs 1.80 EUR. The system uses 1.80 from bonus first (consumption priority). No credit is consumed &mdash; so no VAT is due on this play.</li>
        <li>Next game: 1.80 EUR again. Bonus is only 0.20 left, so 0.20 from bonus + 1.60 from credit. VAT is calculated on exactly 1.60 &mdash; not 1.80.</li>
        <li>Later, the customer uses credit to pay for a birthday party. Different VAT rate. The system handles it.</li>
        <li>The customer also buys food with their credit. Different VAT rate again. Handled.</li>
        <li>Some credit expires after 18 months. That expired credit needs to be accounted for too.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Every single transaction needs to know: how much credit was consumed, at what VAT rate, and for what type of service. The system tracks this automatically, in real time, for every play, every purchase, every partial balance consumption.</p>

    <p><strong>Third, it breaks your reporting.</strong> When a top-up is no longer a sale for accounting purposes, your sales reports and your accounting reports will show different numbers &mdash; and they should. A 10 EUR top-up is revenue from an operational perspective, but it's not a taxable sale until the credit is used. So now you need two views of the same data: one for operations (how much money came in today) and one for accounting (how much VAT-liable revenue was generated today). Most systems can barely produce one correct report. Sapiens produces both, automatically, from the same underlying data &mdash; because it tracks the distinction at the transaction level.</p>

    <div class="page-footer">
        <span class="confidential">SapiensCore &bull; Confidential</span>
        <span>Page 6</span>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page page-break">
    <h3>What Sapiens does</h3>

    <p>Sapiens handles all of this for you. Completely.</p>

    <div class="value-prop">
        <div class="value-prop-title">VAT-Postponed Credit (Credit-VAT)</div>
        <p>When enabled, Sapiens separates the top-up moment from the taxation moment. Credit loaded onto a card is stored as <strong>VAT-postponed</strong> &mdash; no VAT is calculated, no VAT is declared, no VAT is paid to the tax authority. VAT is only calculated at the exact moment the credit is consumed &mdash; on the exact amount consumed &mdash; at the correct VAT rate for the specific product or service.</p>
    </div>

    <p><strong>You have to do literally nothing.</strong></p>

    <p>The system handles the consumption priority, the partial amounts, the different VAT rates, the bonus separation, the expiration accounting, and the fiscal declarations. It generates the correct data automatically: because you also need to account for the credit-VAT in your books. Your accounting team sees clean, correct numbers. Your tax declarations are compliant.</p>

    <div style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin: 25px 0;"></div>

    <h3>Why this matters more than most features combined</h3>

    <p>Everyone in this industry talks about how to increase revenue by 20%, 30%. They tell you to add bigger packages, run promotions, increase the bonus percentage or buy entire new set of hardware to accept more payment methods.</p>

    <p>And they're not wrong &mdash; but they're only looking at one side.</p>

    <p><strong>No one talks about the money you're already losing.</strong> Not from theft, not from fraud &mdash; from paying VAT on credit that was never used. It's invisible. It doesn't show up as a loss in any report. But it's real, and it compounds every single day, on every single card, across every single location.</p>

    <div class="callout" style="border-left-color: var(--primary); background: #f0f1fa;">
        <strong>This is what we mean by "designed for what's next."</strong><br><br>
        We don't only look at what you can sell more of. We look at every single aspect of your operation &mdash; including the ones nobody else is examining &mdash; and find where value is being left on the table. Credit-VAT is the clearest example: a feature that exists because someone actually sat down, understood how this business works at the deepest level, and built a solution that no one else offers.<br><br>
        From our investigation, <strong>essentially no other system in this industry provides this capability.</strong>
    </div>

    <div class="page-footer">
        <span class="confidential">SapiensCore &bull; Confidential</span>
        <span>Page 7</span>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page page-break">
