    <h3>Card Technology &mdash; RFID, NFC, and Custom Firmware</h3>
    <p>Sapiens supports <strong>RFID and NFC cards</strong>. But what makes the difference is <em>how</em> we support them.</p>

    <p>For every terminal where card reading is involved &mdash; whether it's a PAX iM25 or iM30 at a game machine, or the classic POS terminal at the counter &mdash; <strong>we write the firmware ourselves</strong>. The integration, the card reading logic, the communication protocol: all built internally.</p>

    <p>This is another difference. We outsource less-critical features when it makes sense, but the core &mdash; the firmware that controls how your devices read, validate, and interact with cards &mdash; we build in-house. That's why we can confidently say: <strong>we can read any card that runs on RFID or NFC technology</strong>, as long as you provide us the technical specifications.</p>

    <div class="callout" style="border-left-color: var(--accent);">
        <strong>This becomes incredibly powerful</strong> when you reach the chapter about POS and payment terminals. Because when you control the firmware, you control the experience &mdash; and the possibilities are far beyond what off-the-shelf integrations can offer. It was genuinely hard to build. But now that it's done, it's one of our biggest advantages.
    </div>

    <p>The system also supports <strong>service and test cards</strong> for staff use and maintenance operations, kept separate from customer cards. Though as you'll discover later in this document &mdash; you might not need them at all.</p>

