<div class="page page-break">
    <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 12</div>
        <h2>Mobile Payment &mdash; QR Code &amp; NFC Tap-to-Pay</h2>
        <p>No app. No card. Just a phone. And the game starts.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="section-intro">
        This is one of the most requested features in the industry. And one that others sell as a separate product, through a partner, with a monthly fee per game. With Sapiens, it's built in. All you need is a PulseBox on the game. No extra hardware. No monthly per-game fee.
    </p>

    <h3>How It Works for the Customer</h3>

    <p>On the arcade machine, there's a small card with a <strong>QR code and an NFC tag</strong>. The customer can either scan the QR code with their phone camera or &mdash; even easier &mdash; just <strong>tap their phone on the NFC tag</strong>.</p>

    <p style="font-size: 10pt; color: var(--text-light);">
        You can print the QR codes yourself &mdash; Sapiens provides an easy way to generate and print them, simplified for bulk production. Or design your own, in your own style, however you want. We also offer <strong>custom business-card-sized cards</strong> with QR code, NFC chip, your custom design, full-colour print, high-quality finish, and 3M self-adhesive backing &mdash; priced per card between 2.00 and 2.50 EUR one off paymetn per card. Or get them from any other provider. As always: no lock-in. The QR code also has a second function that we'll explain in a later chapter &mdash; for now, think from the customer's perspective.
    </p>

    <p>A mobile-optimised webpage opens instantly. No app download. No account creation. It shows:</p>

    <ul class="clean">
        <li>The location they're at</li>
        <li>The game they tapped</li>
        <li>The price</li>
        <li>Payment options &mdash; <strong>Apple Pay or Google Pay</strong> (automatically detected based on the device) plus manual card entry if they prefer</li>
    </ul>

    <p>They tap to pay. The game starts. That's it.</p>

    <h3>How It Works Behind the Scenes</h3>

    <p>The flow is designed to be bulletproof &mdash; the customer never pays for a game that doesn't start:</p>

    <ol class="clean">
        <li><strong>Quick check:</strong> Sapiens verifies the PulseBox is online and the game is available. If not, the customer sees a clear message &mdash; no payment is attempted.</li>
        <li><strong>Pre-authorisation:</strong> The payment is pre-authorised (held, not charged). The money is reserved but not taken yet.</li>
        <li><strong>Game start:</strong> Sapiens sends the start command to the PulseBox. The relay fires, the game starts.</li>
        <li><strong>Confirmation:</strong> If the game started successfully, the pre-auth is captured &mdash; now the payment is finalised.</li>
        <li><strong>Failure protection:</strong> If the game fails to start for any reason, the pre-auth is <strong>released automatically</strong>. The customer is never charged for a game that didn't work.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="callout" style="border-left-color: var(--accent);">
        <strong>No iM25 needed. No Nayax needed. Just a PulseBox and a sticker.</strong> This makes mobile payment accessible for every game in your venue, including machines where installing a payment terminal isn't practical or cost-effective. The PulseBox is affordable, and there's no monthly fee per game. Compare that with competitors who charge a per-game monthly subscription through a third-party partner &mdash; adding yet another system, another contract, another integration to manage.
    </div>

    <h3>Online Payment Processor</h3>
    <p>The online payment processing can use whatever provider you want. We can also provide one. Currently integrated with Stripe &mdash; which means Apple Pay, Google Pay, and all major card networks are supported out of the box. But if you already have a preferred payment processor, we can work with that.</p>

    <h3>Nayax Integration</h3>
    <p>SapiensCore fully supports Nayax cashless payment terminals. If your venue already uses Nayax &mdash; or plans to &mdash; the integration is seamless:</p>

    <div class="callout" style="border-left-color: var(--accent);">
        <strong>Near real-time sales sync.</strong> As soon as a transaction is processed by Nayax, it becomes available in SapiensCore. Sales data flows in almost instantly, giving you a unified, up-to-the-minute view of all revenue &mdash; whether from Nayax terminals, PAX terminals, loyalty cards, or mobile NFC payments.
    </div>

    <ul class="clean">
        <li><strong>Full loyalty card support on Nayax:</strong> customers can use any SapiensCore loyalty card on Nayax terminals, exactly as they would on any other payment point</li>
        <li>Nayax POS terminal registration and management within the SapiensCore admin panel</li>
        <li>Transaction aggregation alongside all other payment methods in unified sales analytics and reporting</li>
        <li>Nayax actor hierarchy mapping for multi-location organizations</li>
        <li>Automatic fiscal allocation for Nayax transactions (tax compliance)</li>
        <li>Journal entry generation from Nayax sales</li>
    </ul>

