<div class="page page-break">
    <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 08</div>
        <h2>QR Code &amp; NFC Mobile Payment</h2>
        <p>Scan, pay, play &mdash; from any smartphone, on any arcade machine.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="section-intro">
        SapiensCore's mobile payment system lets customers pay for arcade games directly from their smartphones. A QR code on the machine links to a Stripe-powered checkout &mdash; no app download required, no loyalty card needed. The game starts automatically after payment confirmation.
    </p>

    <h3>The Payment Flow</h3>
    <div class="flow-diagram">
        <div class="flow-step">Scan QR Code</div>
        <span class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</span>
        <div class="flow-step">Verify PulseBox Online</div>
        <span class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</span>
        <div class="flow-step" style="background: var(--accent-dark);">Stripe Pre-Auth</div>
        <span class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</span>
        <div class="flow-step">Customer Confirms</div>
        <span class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</span>
        <div class="flow-step" style="background: var(--success);">Game Starts</div>
        <span class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</span>
        <div class="flow-step">Capture Payment</div>
    </div>

    <h4>Step-by-Step</h4>
    <table class="data-table">
        <tr>
            <th style="width:8%;">Step</th>
            <th style="width:20%;">Action</th>
            <th>Detail</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>1</td>
            <td><strong>Scan QR</strong></td>
            <td>Customer scans the QR code displayed on the arcade machine with their phone's camera. Opens a payment page in their mobile browser &mdash; no app needed.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>2</td>
            <td><strong>Verify Online</strong></td>
            <td>SapiensCore checks that the associated PulseBox is online and responsive via daemon-core. If the device is offline, the customer is informed before any charge.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>3</td>
            <td><strong>Pre-Auth</strong></td>
            <td>A Stripe pre-authorization (hold) is placed on the customer's card. No charge is finalized yet. Supports SCA/3D Secure for European compliance.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>4</td>
            <td><strong>Confirm</strong></td>
            <td>Customer reviews the game and price, then confirms. SapiensCore sends the start command to PulseBox.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>5</td>
            <td><strong>Game Starts</strong></td>
            <td>PulseBox activates its relay, starting the game. The game-start result is recorded.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>6</td>
            <td><strong>Capture</strong></td>
            <td>Only after the game successfully starts does SapiensCore capture (finalize) the pre-authorized payment.</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <div class="highlight-box">
        <p><strong>Automatic refund guarantee:</strong> If the game fails to start after payment (PulseBox reports failure, timeout, or device goes offline), the pre-authorized hold is released automatically. The customer is never charged for a game that didn't start. This is tracked via the STATUS_GAME_FAILED and STATUS_REFUNDED states.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-footer">
        <span class="confidential">SapiensCore &bull; Confidential</span>
        <span>Page 16</span>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page page-break">
    <h3>NFC Payment Status Lifecycle</h3>
    <p>Every mobile payment transitions through a precisely defined state machine:</p>

    <table class="data-table">
        <tr>
            <th>Status</th>
            <th>Meaning</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Pending</strong></td>
            <td>Customer has scanned the QR code and the payment page is loaded. No charge yet.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Paid</strong></td>
            <td>Stripe pre-authorization succeeded. Awaiting game start confirmation.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Game Started</strong></td>
            <td>PulseBox confirmed the game started successfully. Payment captured.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Game Failed</strong></td>
            <td>PulseBox reported the game failed to start. Pre-auth released.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Expired</strong></td>
            <td>The payment session timed out before the customer completed checkout.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Payment Failed</strong></td>
            <td>The Stripe charge was declined or encountered an error.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Refunded</strong></td>
            <td>A completed payment was refunded (post-capture refund).</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Wallet &amp; Payment Method Support</h3>
    <div class="feature-grid">
        <div class="feature-item">
            <div class="feature-item-title">Apple Pay</div>
            Detected automatically. Customers with Apple Pay enabled can complete payment in seconds with Face ID or Touch ID.
