    <p class="section-intro">
        Each QR code in SapiensCore represents a unique entry point for mobile payment. The platform provides tools for generating, organizing, and deploying QR codes across venues at scale.
    </p>

    <h3>QR Code Lifecycle</h3>
    <table class="data-table">
        <tr>
            <th>Stage</th>
            <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Generation</strong></td>
            <td>QR codes are generated individually or in bulk batches. Each gets a unique identifier and URL.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Sequencing</strong></td>
            <td>Codes are organized into numbered sequences for systematic deployment across game floors.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Assignment</strong></td>
            <td>Each QR code is linked to a specific PulseBox (QR-to-NFC assignment), connecting it to a physical game machine.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Deployment</strong></td>
            <td>Printed QR codes are placed on arcade machines. Scanning triggers the mobile payment flow.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Monitoring</strong></td>
            <td>Payment history per QR code is tracked, showing usage volume and success rates.</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Bulk Operations</h3>
    <div class="two-col">
        <div class="value-prop">
            <div class="value-prop-title">Bulk QR Generation</div>
            <p>Generate dozens or hundreds of QR codes in a single operation. Each code is assigned a sequence number and stored with metadata for tracking.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="value-prop">
            <div class="value-prop-title">Organized Deployment</div>
            <p>QR code sequences enable systematic floor-by-floor deployment. Staff can match sequence numbers to game positions for fast installation.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h3>Analytics per QR Code</h3>
    <p>SapiensCore tracks payment history per QR code, enabling analysis of:</p>
    <ul class="clean">
        <li>Total payments processed through each QR code</li>
        <li>Success vs. failure rates (identifying problematic PulseBox connections)</li>
        <li>Revenue generated per game machine via mobile payments</li>
        <li>Customer payment method preferences (Apple Pay vs. Google Pay vs. card)</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="highlight-box">
        <p><strong>Aggregated NFC revenue reports</strong> are available by location and by game, enabling operators to compare mobile payment adoption across venues and identify games that benefit most from QR-code-based payment.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-footer">
        <span class="confidential">SapiensCore &bull; Confidential</span>
        <span>Page 18</span>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page page-break">
    <h3>QR Code &amp; PulseBox Integration Architecture</h3>

    <p>The relationship between QR codes, PulseBoxes, games, and locations forms a clean data model that enables both flexibility and traceability:</p>

    <div class="value-prop">
        <div class="value-prop-title">Data Relationships</div>
        <p><strong>QR Code</strong> &rarr; links to &rarr; <strong>PulseBox</strong> &rarr; installed on &rarr; <strong>Game at Location</strong></p>
        <p>When a customer scans a QR code, SapiensCore resolves the full chain: which PulseBox, which game, which location, what price &mdash; all from a single scan.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Game Performance via NFC Payments</h3>
    <p>SapiensCore aggregates NFC payment data to provide game-level performance insights:</p>

    <div class="feature-grid">
