<!-- =====================================================================
     PAGE 20-21: GAME MANAGEMENT
     ====================================================================== -->
<div class="page page-break">
    <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 10</div>
        <h2>Game Management &amp; Configuration</h2>
        <p>Per-location game setup, pricing strategies, and acceptor management.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="section-intro">
        SapiensCore maintains a centralized game catalog while enabling per-location configuration of pricing, payment acceptance, and device mapping. This architecture allows a game to have different prices at different venues, accept different payment methods, and connect to different hardware &mdash; all managed from a single admin interface.
    </p>

    <h3>Game Catalog</h3>
    <p>The game catalog is the master list of all game titles across the organization. Each entry defines:</p>
    <ul class="clean">
        <li>Game name and identification</li>
        <li>Default pricing (overridable at the location level)</li>
        <li>Game category and type classification</li>
        <li>Acceptor configuration (which payment types the game supports)</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Per-Location Configuration</h3>
    <p>When a game is deployed at a specific location, SapiensCore creates a <strong>Game Location</strong> record that allows location-level customization:</p>

    <table class="data-table">
        <tr>
            <th>Configuration</th>
            <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Location-Specific Pricing</strong></td>
            <td>Override the default game price for a specific venue. Enable different pricing strategies based on market, competition, or customer demographics.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Game Acceptor</strong></td>
            <td>Define which payment types this game accepts at this location: loyalty card, bank card terminal, mobile QR/NFC, cash.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Device Mapping</strong></td>
            <td>Link the game to specific hardware: which PulseBox, which payment terminal, which NUC handles transactions.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Default Configuration</strong></td>
            <td>Game Location Defaults allow batch-setting configurations that apply to all games at a location unless overridden.</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Game Acceptor System</h3>
    <p>The acceptor system controls what payment methods each game will recognize:</p>

    <div class="feature-grid">
        <div class="feature-item">
            <div class="feature-item-title">Acceptor Profiles</div>
            Define reusable payment acceptance profiles (e.g., "Card + Loyalty" or "All Methods") that can be assigned to multiple games.
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item">
            <div class="feature-item-title">Location-Level Acceptors</div>
            Override acceptor profiles at the location level, enabling venues to support different payment configurations.
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item">
            <div class="feature-item-title">Acceptor Collections</div>
            Group multiple acceptor configurations into collections for efficient management of large game floors.
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item">
            <div class="feature-item-title">Terminal Mapping</div>
            1:1 mapping (one terminal per game) for attended setups, or 1:many (one terminal serving multiple games) for unattended multi-game stations.
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page-footer">
        <span class="confidential">SapiensCore &bull; Confidential</span>
        <span>Page 20</span>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page page-break">
    <h3>Game Pricing Strategies</h3>
    <p>SapiensCore supports flexible pricing strategies that can vary by location, time, and customer tier:</p>

    <ul class="clean">
        <li><strong>Standard pricing:</strong> Fixed price per game play, consistent across all customers</li>
        <li><strong>Location-specific pricing:</strong> Different prices at different venues based on market conditions</li>
        <li><strong>Tier-based discounts:</strong> Loyalty tier members receive automatic discounts applied at the transaction level</li>
        <li><strong>Package-based play:</strong> Time-based packages that provide unlimited play within a duration window</li>
        <li><strong>Match-limited packages:</strong> Packages that include a fixed number of plays across all games or per-game limits</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Game Location History</h3>
    <p>SapiensCore tracks the history of each game at each location, recording:</p>
    <ul class="clean">
        <li>When the game was installed at the location</li>
        <li>Configuration changes over time</li>
        <li>Hardware assignments (which PulseBox, which terminal)</li>
        <li>Staff assignments for the game area</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="highlight-box primary">
        <p><strong>Data-driven decisions:</strong> By tracking game history alongside performance data (revenue, play count, failure rates), operators can make informed decisions about game rotation, placement optimization, and investment in new titles.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-footer">
        <span class="confidential">SapiensCore &bull; Confidential</span>
        <span>Page 21</span>
    </div>
</div>

