<div class="page page-break">
    <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 14</div>
        <h2>Reservation System</h2>
        <p>Online booking, capacity management, and payment tracking for every activity.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="section-intro">
        SapiensCore's reservation system manages the complete booking lifecycle for entertainment venue activities &mdash; from online customer booking through check-in, completion, and payment reconciliation. It supports birthday parties, jump sessions, bowling lanes, and any other bookable activity.
    </p>

    <h3>Reservation Statuses</h3>
    <table class="data-table">
        <tr>
            <th>Status</th>
            <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Pending</strong></td>
            <td>Reservation submitted, awaiting confirmation. Capacity is tentatively held.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Confirmed</strong></td>
            <td>Reservation approved by staff or auto-confirmed. Capacity is committed.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Checked In</strong></td>
            <td>Customer has arrived and been checked in at the venue.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Completed</strong></td>
            <td>Activity has been delivered. Ready for final payment reconciliation.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Cancelled</strong></td>
            <td>Reservation cancelled by customer or staff. Capacity released.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>No-Show</strong></td>
            <td>Customer did not arrive. Triggers no-show tracking for analytics.</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <h3>Payment Tracking</h3>
    <p>Every reservation tracks payment status independently from booking status:</p>

    <table class="data-table">
        <tr>
            <th>Payment Status</th>
            <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Unpaid</strong></td>
            <td>No payment received yet</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Authorization</strong></td>
            <td>Card pre-authorized but not captured</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Pending</strong></td>
            <td>Payment processing is in progress</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Partially Paid</strong></td>
            <td>Deposit received, balance outstanding</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Paid</strong></td>
            <td>Full payment received</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Refunded</strong></td>
            <td>Payment returned to customer (cancellation, etc.)</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <div class="page-footer">
        <span class="confidential">SapiensCore &bull; Confidential</span>
        <span>Page 26</span>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page page-break">
    <h3>Capacity &amp; Hold System</h3>
    <p>SapiensCore manages venue capacity with a hold/blocking system that prevents overbooking:</p>
    <ul class="clean">
        <li><strong>Reservation holds</strong> temporarily block capacity during the booking process</li>
        <li><strong>Calendar-based availability</strong> shows real-time slot availability across time slots and activities</li>
        <li><strong>Opening hours integration</strong> ensures bookings only appear during operational hours</li>
        <li><strong>Holiday management</strong> with special availability rules for holidays and peak periods</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Sync with External Systems</h3>
    <p>Reservations support synchronization with external booking platforms:</p>
    <ul class="clean">
        <li><strong>Sync status tracking:</strong> Pending, Synced, or Failed &mdash; for each external system</li>
        <li><strong>Bi-directional updates</strong> ensure consistency between SapiensCore and third-party booking platforms</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Voucher Integration</h3>
    <p>Customers can apply voucher codes during the reservation process. SapiensCore validates the voucher, tracks usage, and adjusts the payment amount accordingly. The voucher-to-reservation link is maintained for reporting.</p>

