<div class="page page-break">
    <h3>Integration Architecture</h3>
    <p>SapiensCore's integration layer is designed for reliability and observability:</p>

    <div class="feature-grid">
        <div class="feature-item">
            <div class="feature-item-title">Outbound Queues</div>
            Each external integration (Odoo, Nayax, SII) has a dedicated outbound queue with status tracking. Failed deliveries are retried automatically with exponential backoff.
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item">
            <div class="feature-item-title">Webhook Processing</div>
            Incoming webhooks (Stripe, Ethoca) are processed asynchronously via SQS to ensure reliable handling without blocking request threads.
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item">
            <div class="feature-item-title">API Request Logging</div>
            All inbound and outbound API calls are logged with request/response payloads for debugging and audit purposes.
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item">
            <div class="feature-item-title">Health Monitoring</div>
            Integration health is monitored through the cron job status system, with alerts when sync jobs fail or queues back up.
        </div>
    </div>

    <h3>Notification Architecture</h3>
    <p>SapiensCore provides a multi-channel notification system:</p>
    <ul class="clean">
        <li><strong>System notifications:</strong> In-app notifications for admin users, managed per-user</li>
        <li><strong>Email notifications:</strong> Automated emails for customer-facing events via Mailgun</li>
        <li><strong>Push notifications:</strong> Browser push via daemon-core for real-time device alerts</li>
        <li><strong>Mobile push:</strong> Firebase for customer mobile app notifications</li>
