<!-- =====================================================================
     PAGE 49: TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE
     ====================================================================== -->
<div class="page page-break">
    <div class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-number">Chapter 28</div>
        <h2>Technical Architecture</h2>
        <p>Built for scale, reliability, and multi-tenant operations.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Core Architecture</h3>
    <table class="data-table">
        <tr>
            <th>Component</th>
            <th>Technology &amp; Purpose</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Backend</strong></td>
            <td>PHP with modern architecture. REST API with versioning (V1) and multiple namespaces.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Database</strong></td>
            <td>PostgreSQL with materialized views for fast analytics and full-text search capabilities.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Caching</strong></td>
            <td>Redis for real-time data caching (loyalty tiers, device status, session data). Sub-millisecond lookups for transaction-critical data.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Containerization</strong></td>
            <td>Docker-based deployment for consistent environments across development, staging, and production.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Real-Time</strong></td>
            <td>Cloudflare Workers with WebSocket for daemon-core device monitoring and command dispatch.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Async Processing</strong></td>
            <td>AWS SQS for background task processing: report generation, ERP sync, bulk operations.</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <h3>API Architecture</h3>
    <p>SapiensCore exposes multiple API namespaces for different client types:</p>

    <div class="feature-grid">
        <div class="feature-item">
            <div class="feature-item-title">Admin API</div>
            Full platform management for the admin panel. All CRUD operations, reporting, and configuration.
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item">
            <div class="feature-item-title">SapiensClient API</div>
            Customer-facing API for loyalty card operations, mobile payments, and customer account management.
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item">
            <div class="feature-item-title">PDA API</div>
            API for handheld devices used by floor staff for mobile operations and quick lookups.
        </div>
        <div class="feature-item">
            <div class="feature-item-title">Workstation API</div>
            API for fixed venue devices: POS terminals, kiosks, and counter workstations.
        </div>
    </div>

    <h3>Batch Processing</h3>
    <p>SapiensCore runs 30+ automated cron jobs that handle recurring tasks:</p>
    <ul class="clean">
        <li>Credit expiration processing</li>
        <li>ERP synchronization (Odoo journal entries, payments, refunds)</li>
        <li>Materialized view refresh for analytics</li>
        <li>Device health monitoring and alerting</li>
        <li>Report generation and distribution</li>
        <li>Data cleanup and archival</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Each cron job's status is tracked and visible in the admin panel, with alerting when jobs fail.</p>

    <div class="page-footer">
